From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: player-led Dolby Vision

The Vulkan engine maps Dolby Vision to the TV's own peak, black and
primaries (DVVK_OUTPUT_LLDV, CroqueMr's CB1 "LLDV Reference - Native")
and this tree's kernel signals it (DVBRIDGE_TUNNEL_FORMAT lldv: the
Dolby VSIF with its low-latency bit, AVI YCbCr 4:2:2 BT.2020 limited
range, no HDR static metadata), but Kodi could not ask for either.

Output mode gets "Dolby Vision (player-led)" (OutputMode::PlayerLed,
5), in the setting and in the video OSD's list, offered only where:
- the engine library has the mode (dvvk_output_modes,
  dvvk_set_display_primaries, dvvk_lldv_display_from_vsvdb);
- the connector has the lldv value of DVBRIDGE_TUNNEL_FORMAT, at
  progressive 3840x2160;
- the TV's Dolby Vision VSVDB has the low-latency interface by the
  kernel's own test, and dvvk_lldv_display_from_vsvdb gives a target
  from it (CDisplayInfo now keeps the block's bytes).
kodi.log says which condition fails when the answer changes.

Playing, the window begins the tunnel with the target; the engine sets
the TV's primaries and version, then the mode with its peak and black
(DV_LLDV_BITS=10: DVVK_LLDV_10BIT), and sends each frame with no
dm_options (the engine refuses CM4.0 and L2 removal for it). The
commit of a player-led picture stages the lldv format with no HDR
metadata and no HDR10+. Player information shows the output and the
TV's target.

It is never chosen by the Automatic fallback, and where it is not
available the video falls back as Dolby Vision does on a TV without
it: Convert to HDR10, then SDR. If the engine refuses the TV's target,
or the kernel refuses ten player-led commits in a row, it is withdrawn
until Kodi restarts (notification) and the title restarts with that
fallback; no picture of another kind is sent meanwhile.
DV_LLDV_OUTPUT=0 removes it.

Not yet seen on a display. With Output mode at any other value no new
engine call is made and no new connector property is written.

Strings 45167 to 45170; the Output mode help (45015) describes it.
